// A lamp somebody carries, and the first thing in the game that belongs
// to a *person* rather than to the tower.
//
// **This is what "equip" means here.** The obvious reading — weapons
// bolted to the building — is a different game, and the tower's half of
// it already exists: what you feed a dart battery *is* the choice. A kit
// is the other half. `DESIGN.md` §2 structural call 4 says crew are
// named individuals and not stat blocks, and a kit is the smallest
// mechanic that makes that true in the simulation rather than only in
// the fiction — Wren carries the lamp, and you know which of them it is.
//
// What it answers is real and already in the game: `dark_work_pct` is
// 75, so everybody works a quarter slower in a brown-out. A lamp is the
// tower saying "not this one". It does not make the brown-out go away,
// it makes one person able to work through it, which is exactly the
// triage the siege asks for.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
ItemDef(
    id: "item.hand_lamp",
    name: "Hand lamp",
    glyph: "🏮",
    order: 40,
    kit: KitDef(
        lights_the_dark: true,
    ),
)
